<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.4.1: Introducing the Zero Product Property</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02141</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.4.1: Introducing the Zero Product Property</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e9d7613a-4686-419d-8d71-55a3dab73aaf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
        <para id="para-00001"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_8_4_1_WU_15"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
      <para id="para-00021">We will use the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">zero product property</term> to help solve <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">quadratic equations</term> throughout this lesson.</para>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>ZERO PRODUCT PROPERTY</title>
  <para id="para-00022">If the product of two expressions is 0, then one or both of the expressions equal 0.</para>
  <para id="para-00023">If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>